## Interface: 20506
## Title: Popperpig Raid Call
## Notes: Raid-leader command surface for Mount Hyjal and Black Temple.|nOwns the twenty minutes around the fight, not the three minutes in it.
## Author: bfrenchy
## Version: @project-version@
## SavedVariables: PopperpigRaidCallDB
## X-License: MIT
## X-Category: Raid Frames
## DefaultState: Enabled

# Set this once the CurseForge project exists (see README, "Publishing to CurseForge"):
# ## X-Curse-Project-ID: 000000

# --- Core ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Init must load first: it owns the namespace, the event bus and the DB.
# Adapter must load second: every module below it probes capabilities through it.
Core\Init.lua
Core\Adapter.lua
Core\Codec.lua
Core\RateLimit.lua
Core\StateMachine.lua

# --- Data ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Pure tables, zero logic. NPC IDs and wave compositions live ONLY here, so a
# patch fix is a data edit that can ship the same night.
Data\Consumables.lua
Data\Calls.lua
Data\Positions.lua
Data\Hyjal.lua
Data\BlackTemple.lua

# --- Core that consumes Data --------------------------------------------
Core\Detect.lua
Core\Roster.lua
Core\Comm.lua

# --- UI -----------------------------------------------------------------
# All plain CreateFrame("Frame"). No secure templates, so none of this can taint.
UI\Widgets.lua
UI\PosMap.lua
UI\HUD.lua
UI\CallBoard.lua
UI\Readiness.lua
UI\Roster.lua
UI\Briefing.lua
UI\Options.lua

# --- Commands last: it wires every module above into /pprc ---------------
Core\Commands.lua
